## A. Documents that govern, and why

- NAVFAC is the construction agent, so FC 1-300-09N (2024, with Change 1) is the governing design procedures criteria. Its paragraph 12-3.3.4 sets the CAD order of precedence: the FC chapter itself first, then the latest A/E/C CAD and Graphics Standards, then the National CAD Standard. That clause is also why Release 6.2 of the A/E/C CAD Standard is applied and the Release 6.0 file in the folder is set aside.
- The Contracting Officer memorandum of 26 August 2026 (paragraph 7) adopts ER 1165-2-217 and ERDC/ITL SR-21-6 for the design-review conventions only (four-part comment, concur/non-concur response and closure, markup colours, statement of every affected location) and expressly brings in nothing else, in particular no record-package deliverable requirement.
- ER 415-1-11 is the review regulation the memorandum (paragraph 3) points to for when the backcheck is conducted and when comments must be resolved. FAR 52.236-25 (prescribed by FAR 36.609-4) and FC 1-300-09N paragraph 2-5 tie design review, approval and sealing to registration in the particular professional field.
- Dates: BP-2 was advertised 6 July 2026 with bid opening 28 September 2026 (solicitation schedule). BP-3 bid opening is 12 November 2026; its advertisement date is 9 November 2026 per memorandum paragraph 3, which controls over the 12 October 2026 date in the earlier schedule export.
- Rejected: A/E/C CAD Standard Release 6.0 (superseded), UFC 1-300-09N of 2005 (cancelled), GSA PBS CAD Standards (another agency), ER 1110-1-8159 (DrChecks administration, not adopted), the fire protection comment log (separate task order and discipline) and the FY23 record drawings (reference only).

